From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:26:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] arm: dts: meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot: set vddio_c
 to 3.3V

vddio_c (RK818 LDO9) is the vqmmc supply of the SD card. Linux picks
3.0V for it, and after a reboot from Linux U-Boot finds it still at
3.0V: the card initializes, but data reads fail, so the kernel cannot
be loaded and the board drops to the U-Boot prompt. A cold boot works
since the PMIC starts from its 3.3V default.

Set it to 3.3V when U-Boot probes the regulator.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
index 1c0f9765..9ae0a50c 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/meson-g12b-odroid-go-ultra-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -22,3 +22,11 @@
 &vdd_ee {
 	regulator-init-microvolt = <875000>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * vddio_c supplies the SD card I/O. Linux may leave it at 3.0V across a
+ * reboot, where SD card reads fail in U-Boot; start from 3.3V.
+ */
+&vddio_c {
+	regulator-init-microvolt = <3300000>;
+};
